--
--   Description
----------------
--   This test ensures that the GEM Ability match functionality works properly.

-- Detailed Test Description
--
--  Note: This is an overall description of the test below.  
-- 1.  Initialise the GEM for Gigabit Operation with PCS enabled. Furthermore, Auto-Negotiation is 
--     enabled.
-- 2.  Once the GEM enters AN_ENABLE state, it should start transmitting alternating /C/ codes with 
--     the Config_Reg field all zeros.
-- 3.  Provide a stream of /C/ codes with a Config_Reg of all zero. 
-- 4.  Provide a stream of /C/ codes where Config_Reg takes on any value. 
-- 5.  Repeat step (1) and (4) varying the Config_Reg<D15:0> value.
-- 6.  Provide a stream of /C/ codes where two Config_Reg<D15:0> values (which are 1 bit different) are 
--     sent repeatedly.
-- 7.  Observe transmission from GEM.
-- 8.  Repeat step (6) and (7) varying the Config_Reg value such that only 1 bit is ever different,
--     but all 16 bits are eventually tested.
-- 9.  Restart auto-negotiation by any means.
-- 10. Provide a stream of /I/ codes to the GEM. Continue until the GEM sources a non-zero Config_Reg value.
-- 11. Source a sequence of (x) consecutive and identical Config_Reg values, followed by a stream of /I/ codes. 
--     (x) is initially 1.
-- 12. Repeat step (9) through (11), increasing (x) until the device sets its ACK bit.
-- 13. Repeat step (9) and (10) and source a sequence of (x-1) consecutive and identical Config_Reg values 
--     followed by an /I/ code, followed by (y) Config_Reg values
--     identical to the previous, followed by a stream of /I/ codes. (y) is initially 1.
-- 14. Repeat step (13), increasing (y) until the device sets its ACK bit.
-- 15. Repeat step (9) and (10) and source a sequence of (x-1) consecutive and identical Config_Reg values 
--     followed by a different Config_Reg value, followed by (y)
--     Config_Reg values identical to the initial value, followed by a stream of /I/ codes. (y) is initially 1.
-- 16. Repeat step (15), increasing (y) until the device sets its ACK bit.
--
--   Observable Results:
--
-- a. In step (3), the GEM should not set its ACK bit upon detection of ability_match= TRUE*rx_Config_Reg<D15:D0>=0
-- b. In step (4) and (5), the GEM should set its ACK bit in all cases.
-- c. In step (6),(7) and (8), the GEM should not set its ACK bit upon reception of inconsistent Config_Reg values, with the exception of Config_Reg values that differ
--    only by bit 14 (ACK).
-- d. In step (12), the GEM should set its ACK bit after three identical and consecutive Config_Reg values are received, ie (x)=3.
-- e. In step (14), the GEM should set its ACK bit only after three identical and consecutive Config_Reg values are received, ie (y)=3.
-- f. In step (16), the GEM should set its ACK bit only after three identical and consecutive Config_Reg values are received, ie (y)=3.
--


pinsc(50) loopback 0 half_duplex 1  extint 0 speed 0 --  check reset state


-- ********************************************************************************************* --
-- 1. Initialise the GEM for Gigabit Operation with PCS enabled. Furthermore, Auto-Negotiation is 
--    enabled.
-- ********************************************************************************************* --

-- check and initialise the relevant registers
apbrd(100) 00 00000000  -- check reset value of network control register
apbrd      04 00080000  -- check reset value of network config register
apbrd      08 00000006  -- check reset value of network status register
apbrd     200 00009040  -- check value of pcs control register
apbrd     210 00000020  -- check reset value of pcs auto-nego. adv. register
apbwr     210 00000060  -- pcs auto-nego. adv. register - enable next page bit 
apbrd     210 00000060  -- check pcs auto-nego. adv. register
apbrd     21c 00000000  -- check reset value of pcs auto-nego. next page register

apbwr      04 00081c00  -- Put MAC into gigabit mode with TBI. Retry test enabled
apbrd      04 00081c00  -- Check value of network config register
apbwr      00 00000004  -- enable receive
apbrd      24 00000000  -- check interrupt status
apbwr      28 ffffffff  -- enable all interrupts
apbrd      24 00000000  -- check interrupt status
apbwr      88 03020100  -- specific address register 1 bottom
apbwr      8C 00000504  -- specific address register 1 top
apbrd     200 00001040  -- check value of pcs control register
apbrd     204 00000109  -- check pcs status register
apbrdf     20 00000000  -- check receive status register and trigger reception

